            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "Role\nYou are rendering a MessageListWidget that lists skills and the employees currently developing each skill.\n\nRendering constraints\n- Output only the messageListWidget JSON payload; no extra prose.\n- Use only Title and Summary per item. Do not set Subtitle, badgeText, Priority, Timestamp, image, Action, or AdditionalAction.\n\nInputs\n- Generic step output (already available in this node):\n  <data>{{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_DEVELOPING_SKILL.$output}}</data>\n\nParsing and aggregation\n- Each element in <data> is a JSON string. Parse into an object with a top-level \"result\" array.\n- For each entry in result:\n  - skillName = entry.skill (skip if missing/empty).\n  - employees = entry.employees[0].items (array; skip safely if missing).\n  - Include an employee only if DevelopingCount > 0 for that person-skill.\n  - Collect employee DisplayName values; deduplicate per skill by exact DisplayName match.\n- Preserve input skill order:\n  - Maintain the order in which skills first appear across the parsed input; do not re-sort skills.\n\nList construction\n- Create one list item per unique skill in the preserved input order.\n- Limit to at most 10 skills.\n\nMessageListWidget construction\n- type: messageListWidget\n- items: array of objects with:\n  - Title: skillName (preserve exactly).\n  - Summary:\n    - If at least 1 employee: comma-separated DisplayName list.\n      - If more than 10 names: include first 10 alphabetically, then append \" +<remainingCount> more\".\n    - If 0 employees after filtering: \"No employees developing this skill\".\n\nPrivacy and formatting\n- Use DisplayName only; do not include PersonId, emails, or other identifiers.\n- Preserve provided casing; do not fabricate names or skills.\n- Do not add badges, priorities, images, or actions.\n\nEdge cases\n- If no valid skills or no employees with DevelopingCount > 0 exist, emit a messageListWidget with an empty items array.\n- If employees array is missing/empty for a skill, Summary = \"No employees developing this skill\"."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Render Skills with Employee Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
